// Game: Postretro
// Format: Standard
// Ghost-link acceptance fixture. All coordinates below are Quake map units.
// Two identical room copies: copy A centred at 0 0 and copy B at 4096 0, so the
// copies sit about 104 metres apart, farther than the 60 metre dev mod
// attenuation maxDistance. A real voice in one copy never reaches the other.
// Each copy has an east doorway into a small alcove and a low green cover wall
// west of the doorway. Only the copy A doorway holds the yellow barrier mover.
// Only copy B has the red button switch on its north wall.
// Two ghost links tagged vault_echo, both styled echo. echo_a covers copy A and
// ghosts it into copy B, armed on spawn, listing the barrier tag. echo_b covers
// copy B and ghosts it into copy A, disarmed until the echo plate reveal.
// Barrier puzzle: press the red button in copy B. The barrier in copy A drops
// into the floor, the player in copy B watches its ghost drop in copy B, and the
// player in copy A walks into the alcove. Each link volume reaches below the
// floor so the sinking barrier stays a member until it is out of sight.
// Battle swap: two monsters per copy, passive until the swap. Their descriptor
// does not opt into ghosting, so each player sees only their own monsters plus
// the partner ghost. The purple use pad in either copy arms both seamless swap
// teleporters and rouses every echo monster. Each player then faces the other
// copy monsters. The first teleport through either swap teleporter disarms both.
// The blue touch plate in either copy runs echo.reveal and echo.swell.
// Player spawn 1 is in copy A and spawn 2 in copy B. Body centres are 40 units up.
// An animated-bake lamp in each alcove, tagged alcove_lamp, shines out through
// the doorway. The ghost capture forces it to two colours: the scene around the
// ghost relights, the unlit ghost does not change.
// Cheap bake: one quarter metre per lightmap texel. No compiled output is
// committed.
// NOTE: keep map comments free of braces and quotes, and never leave a blank
// line inside an entity block.
